 through the grid, reflecting it off red line-segment mirrors.\n\nInput structure\n- Black-background grid with one diagonal 8-connected blue ray seed.\n- Red foreground objects, when present, are straight horizontal or vertical mirror segments.\n- Other foreground bars are transparent to the ray and may be overwritten where the ray crosses them.\n\nRule\n- Start from the ray seed endpoint whose outward diagonal extension remains inside the grid.\n- Paint the ray continuously in that diagonal direction until it leaves the grid.\n- If the next cell is a red mirror, do not paint it; reflect by flipping the row direction on a horizontal mirror or the column direction on a vertical mirror.\n\nKey insight\n- The non-red bars are decoys: only red bars reflect the diagonal path, while all other crossed cells become blue.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"diagonal blue ray seed\",\n  \"path\": \"continue from the only in-bounds seed endpoint; red horizontal or vertical bars reflect the diagonal ray; stop when the reflected ray leaves the grid\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint every non-red visited cell blue, overwriting transparent bars\",\n  \"transform\": \"leave red mirror cells unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e734a0e8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3394\nmechanism=0.4195\nlexical=0.0133\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:rotation, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e734a0e8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e734a0e8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nCopy the unique colored sprite tile into every tiled cell marked by an internal separator-colored pixel.\n\nInput structure\n- Full same-color separator rows and columns partition the grid into equal rectangular tiles.\n- One tile contains the only non-background, non-separator colored sprite.\n- Target tiles are otherwise background-colored but contain at least one internal pixel of the separator color.\n\nRule\n- Keep the separator lines and the source sprite tile unchanged.\n- Replace each marked target tile with an exact copy of the source tile.\n- Unmarked background-only tiles remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The internal separator-colored pixels are placement markers; the single colored tile is the template to stamp into those marked cells.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"unique colored sprite tile s in the separator grid\",\n  \"dst\": \"marked background tile d containing an internal separator-colored marker pixel\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"every marked d receives the same unique s\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace d with an exact copy of s, erasing the marker\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"465b7d93\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3497\nmechanism=0.4349\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:line_segment, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/465b7d93.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular\n  one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it.\n- The frame interior is initially background.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the original sprite from its outside location.\n- Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to\n  interior extremes.\n- Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of\n  adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclosed background region inside\n  those drawn segments.\n\nKey insight:\nThe outside sprite is a miniature line/fill diagram for the frame interior,\nnot a bitmap to scale by block replication.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"small colored sprite s outside the frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"hollow rectangular frame interior d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"unique s maps to unique d; s.bbox extremes align to d.bbox extremes\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s; stretch s into d by mapping bbox extremes, drawing 4-adjacent segments, and filling enclosed regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3cd86f4f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3341\nmechanism=0.4277\nlexical=0.0161\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:rotation, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:reflect, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3cd86f4f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3cd86f4f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nShear the rectangular input down-left onto a black canvas.\n\nInput structure\nA rectangular grid of colored pixels with no internal empty region to infer.\n\nRule\nCreate a black output with the same height and width W + H - 1, then copy\neach input row r unchanged starting at column H - 1 - r.\n\nKey insight\nThe colors and row contents are preserved; only the row offsets change so\nthe left edge forms a descending diagonal.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"the full input rectangle, interpreted as rows to be diagonally staggered\",\n  \"dst\": \"black canvas with the same height and enough columns for the staggered rows\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy every row unchanged; place row r starting at column H - 1 - r so adjacent rows shift one column left downward\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"same height, width W + H - 1\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9f669b64\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3511\nmechanism=0.4244\nlexical=0.0125\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:line_segment, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9f669b64.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9f669b64.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPush the central solid rectangle to the grid edge, splitting the perpendicular target rectangle around its path.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly three monochrome foreground objects arranged on one\n  horizontal or vertical axis.\n- The middle object on that axis is a solid rectangular moving object.\n- One end object is a solid rectangle or bar whose long side is perpendicular\n  to the movement axis; this is the target to split.\n\nRule\n- Move the middle rectangle along the axis toward the target until it is\n  flush with the grid edge in that direction.\n- Clear the original middle rectangle and the original target.\n- Split the target through the moving rectangle's two-cell-wide path and\n  shift the two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement.\n- Keep the other end object unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The non-target end object acts as a pusher; the central rectangle travels\n  away from it through the perpendicular target, opening a matching gap.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"middle solid rectangular object between two end objects\",\n  \"path\": \"straight horizontal or vertical line away from the non-target end object and through the perpendicular solid target rectangle/bar\",\n  \"dst\": \"place flush with the grid edge beyond the target\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint only the final moved rectangle at dst\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase original source pixels; split the target rectangle/bar along the moving object's two-cell-wide path and shift its two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement; keep the other end object unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3252\nmechanism=0.3722\nlexical=0.0175\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:marker, object:rectangle, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
